# Function definitions the control value program makes, when one face is
# requested at several sizes in turn: below 12 ppem it defines function 3 to
# push 333 and function 4 to push 444, from 12 ppem only function 4, to push
# 555. The glyph writes what functions 4 and 3 push into the y of points 0
# and 1 (a call of an undefined function ends the program).
sequence 640 1000 640
sequence 1000 640 1000
heights 1000 640
fpgm
  PUSH 0; FDEF; ENDF
end
prep
  MPPEM; PUSH 12; LT
  IF
    PUSH 3; FDEF; PUSH 333; ENDF
    PUSH 4; FDEF; PUSH 444; ENDF
  ELSE
    PUSH 4; FDEF; PUSH 555; ENDF
  EIF
end
glyph advance 1200
  contour 0 0, 100 0, 200 0, 300 0
  program
    SVTCA[0]
    PUSH 0 4; CALL; SCFS
    PUSH 1 3; CALL; SCFS
  end
end
